    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a high-upside slate today, with **Jacob Wilson** leading the charge at a 74.08 efficiency score. Despite the challenging presence of Valdez on the mound, **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a top-of-the-order boost, solidifying his role as our primary offensive engine. **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.88) round out our top-tier plays; **Cole Carrigg** utilizes elite switch-hitting utility against Avila, while **Drake Baldwin** draws a dream matchup against the 4.77 xERA of Mikolas, bolstered by a secure leadoff spot and excellent recent xwOBA metrics. We are also leaning on **Jackson Merrill** (69.09), who enjoys a robust platoon advantage against Mahle, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.51), whose raw base projection remains too high to fade despite a moderate challenge from the lefty Mathews.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Denzer Guzman**, who posted a 44.21 score. While his platoon edge against Gasser was notable, the depth of our middle infield and the aggressive efficiency scores of **Nasim Nunez**\u2014who provides critical speed metrics\u2014pushed him to the bench. Conversely, **Heliot Ramos** (58.70) and **Dominic Smith** (59.48) represent our \"high-floor\" bridge players; while they missed the 60-point threshold for a \"Strong\" start, their matchup reliability against Mikolas and Buehler makes them superior to the volatility of our remaining bench options. Investors should keep a close eye on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; both face a distinct challenge in the form of S\u00e1nchez, whose 2.84 xERA is an elite roadblock. While wind conditions provide a slight +5% boost for them, their individual scores are tempered by the pitcher\u2019s ability to suppress high-speed scoring, making them our most volatile assets for today\u2019s 5x5 rotation.",
